## Finding 2 — Sensitive User Data Exposed Publicly 🔴

**OWASP A01: Broken Access Control**

Even if `/users` were authenticated, it returns **all users to all users** with no ownership or role check. User A should not be able to enumerate User B's data.

**Recommendation:** Scope data to the requesting user, or gate on an admin role:

```js
app.get('/users', requireAuth, (req, res) => {
  // Option A — users can only see themselves
  const user = userService.findById(req.user.sub);
  return res.json(user);
});

app.get('/admin/users', requireAuth, requireRole('admin'), (req, res) => {
  // Option B — only admins get the full list
  const users = userService.findAll();
  return res.json(users);
});

// Role-check middleware
function requireRole(role) {
  return (req, res, next) => {
    if (!req.user.roles?.includes(role)) {
      return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Insufficient permissions' });
    }
    next();
  };
}
```

