### Finding 8 — 🟡 HTTP Only — No HTTPS Enforcement (OWASP A02)

**Location:** `app.listen(3000, ...)`

The server listens on plain HTTP. Credentials and data are transmitted in cleartext.

**Fix:** In production, terminate TLS at a reverse proxy (nginx, AWS ALB, Cloudflare) and enforce HTTPS redirects. Locally, use `https` with self-signed certs:

```js
const https = require('https');
const fs = require('fs');

if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production') {
  // Let your reverse proxy handle TLS; trust it here
  app.set('trust proxy', 1);
} else {
  const options = {
    key: fs.readFileSync('./certs/key.pem'),
    cert: fs.readFileSync('./certs/cert.pem'),
  };
  https.createServer(options, app).listen(3443);
}
```

Also add HSTS via Helmet (`helmet` does this automatically when configured).

