### 7. Verbose Error Handling / Information Leakage (OWASP A09 – Logging & Monitoring Failures)

**Finding:** There is no global error handler. Express's default error handler will dump stack traces to the client in development and may do so in production if `NODE_ENV` isn't set.

**Risk:** Stack traces reveal file paths, library versions, and code structure — a goldmine for attackers.

**Fix:** Add a centralized error handler as the **last middleware**:

```js
// Generic 404 handler
app.use((req, res) => {
  res.status(404).json({ error: 'Route not found' });
});

// Global error handler — must have 4 parameters for Express to treat it as error middleware
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  // Log the full error internally
  console.error({
    message: err.message,
    stack: err.stack,
    url: req.url,
    method: req.method,
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
  });

  // Never send stack traces to the client
  const statusCode = err.status || err.statusCode || 500;
  res.status(statusCode).json({
    error: process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production'
      ? 'An internal error occurred'
      : err.message, // Only show details in non-production
  });
});
```

