### Finding 1 — No Security Headers (OWASP A05)

**Problem:** Express has no security headers by default. Without them, browsers offer no protection against XSS, clickjacking, MIME-sniffing, and more. The current server sends raw Express defaults which actively advertise the framework version.

```js
// What Express sends by default (dangerous):
X-Powered-By: Express   // ← fingerprints your stack for attackers
// Missing entirely:
