The port `3000` is hardcoded. Any real credentials (DB connection strings, API keys, JWT secrets) added in this pattern would be a serious leak risk.

**Recommendation:** Use environment variables via `dotenv`.

```js
require('dotenv').config();

const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;
const JWT_SECRET = process.env.JWT_SECRET;

if (!JWT_SECRET) {
  console.error('FATAL: JWT_SECRET is not set.');
  process.exit(1); // Fail fast — never run without required secrets
}

app.listen(PORT, () => {
  console.log(`Server running on port ${PORT}`);
});
```

And your `.env` file (which must be in `.gitignore`):
```
