### 🟠 HIGH — Missing Security Headers

**Finding:** No HTTP security headers are set. This leaves clients vulnerable to clickjacking, MIME-sniffing, XSS via reflected content, and more.

**OWASP Reference:** [A05:2021 – Security Misconfiguration](https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration/)

**Recommendation:** Add `helmet` — it sets ~14 security headers automatically:

```js
