## 🟡 MEDIUM Findings

### 6. No Input Validation (OWASP A03 – Injection)

**Risk:** The app has no body parser and no validation middleware. When business logic is added (which it will be), there is no established pattern for validating or sanitizing inputs — creating a path for injection attacks (SQL, NoSQL, command injection) and unexpected behavior.

**Recommendation:**
```js
const express = require('express');
const { body, param, query, validationResult } = require('express-validator'); // npm install express-validator

app.use(express.json({ limit: '10kb' })); // parse body AND cap payload size

// Example: validated route
app.get('/users/:id',
  param('id').isInt({ min: 1 }).toInt(),
  (req, res) => {
    const errors = validationResult(req);
    if (!errors.isEmpty()) {
      return res.status(400).json({ errors: errors.array() });
    }
    // safe to use req.params.id now
  }
);
```

