## Finding 5 — 🟡 MEDIUM | No Input Validation or Body Parsing Controls (OWASP A03)

**Location:** Application bootstrap

The app has no `express.json()` / `express.urlencoded()` middleware, and no input validation library. When POST/PUT routes are added (as they inevitably will be), unvalidated input will flow directly into business logic.

```js
// ❌ No body parsing = any future POST handler silently gets req.body === undefined
//    OR if someone adds express.json() without limits:
app.use(express.json()); // unlimited payload — DoS risk
```

**Recommendation:** Add body parsing with size limits and a validation library from day one:

```bash
npm install express-validator
```

```js
